\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A quartic weight at a changing mesh}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The [onsite quartic](fdip-00GJ) multiplies a finite Gaussian law
by a positive weight. The Gaussian variance at a lattice point changes
as the mesh shrinks. Subtracting the corresponding quadratic term and
retaining the constant term ties the quartic to that variance. Which
reference covariance fixes these subtractions when the Gaussian itself
has a boundary? The whole-space and boundary covariances are distinguished
in \citet{(IV.9), (IV.36)-(IV.37)}{guerra1975euclideanII}.}
